    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400 response.\n\nI modified `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the `POST /api/owners` handler):\n\n1. **Added a validation call** at the start of `addOwner`, right after the required-fields check:\n   ```java\n   rejectFutureRegistrationDate(ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\n2. **Added the `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` helper** alongside the other validators:\n   ```java\n   private void rejectFutureRegistrationDate(LocalDate registrationDate) {\n       if (registrationDate != null && registrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {\n           throw new InvalidOwnerFieldsException(List.of(\"registrationDate\"));\n       }\n   }\n   ```\n\nThis reuses the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`, which the `ExceptionControllerAdvice` already maps to **HTTP 400** with the offending field name (`registrationDate`) in the `errors` property \u2014 consistent with how the codebase handles other invalid field values (telephone, email, postcode).\n\nThe check only rejects a *supplied* date that is strictly after today; an absent date still defaults to the server date, and today-or-past dates remain accepted, so existing behavior is preserved.\n\n- `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posts `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"`, expects 400): **passes**\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, all tests green.",
